 o7v f1eueg4z fy9c24f f1h2o91j f1iw08fq f19n0e5"><p><strong>Make Your Voic
 e Heard!</strong></p><p>                                  Join us for an 
 evening of conversation\, learning\, and community as we explore the powe
 r of voting and civic engagement in shaping a more inclusive future for L
 GBTQ+ communities. Our guest speaker (TBD) will share insights on the his
 tory of voting rights\, the impact of collective action\, and why partici
 pation in the 2026 election matters. Whether you're a first-time voter or
  a longtime advocate\, you'll have the opportunity to ask questions\, sha
 re perspectives\, and connect with others who are passionate about making
  a difference.                                </p><p><strong>Ready to tak
 e action? Register to vote!</strong> Visit <strong>www.indianavoters.in.g
 ov</strong> to check your registration status or register to vote (you ca
 n also click on the "register" button below). Follow the LGBTQ+ Culture C
 enter on <strong>QNews\, Facebook\, and Instagram</strong> for voter regi
 stration updates\, election information\, and important deadlines. <stron
 g>The deadline to register to vote in Indiana is October 5\, 2026.</stron
 g></p><p>                                  Come learn\, connect\, and tak
 e the next step toward making your voice count.                          
       </p><p><strong>All Indiana University events\, groups\, activities\
 , educational\, cultural\, and historical observances welcome all members
  of the Indiana University community.</strong></p><p>                    
               &#160\;                                </p></div></div></di
 v></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div
 ></div>
